      "writtenOn": "2022-12-06T02:37:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks a bit odd to me 1) because we always make a copy of AudioHalEngineConfig (when constructing a heap-allocated version), which can be avoided, and 2) when I see `make_unique\u003c\u003e` from a stack-allocated object I suspect that something wrong is going on, also 3) on a general note, classes that need to be managed with a unique_ptr are often not copyable. I would suggest a more canonical implementation instead:\n\n```\nauto tempConfig \u003d std::make_unique\u003cAudioHalEngineConfig\u003e();\nASSERT_IS_OK(mConfig-\u003egetEngineConfig(tempConfig.get()));\nmEngineConfig \u003d std::move(tempConfig);\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 52,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 54,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "435a2a383c4118c801121074da366f1de8b66389",
